Still plugging away towards my first ascension.  Three YASDs over the
weekend:

*  Clawed by a black dragon at Fort Ludios.  Just wasn't paying close
attention to my hit points.  I had a damn potion of full healing on
me, too.  This death was extra heartbreaking because my pet had
stepped onto a polymorph trap early in the game, becoming a kick-ass
silver dragon.  (I'd left him behind because I thought even he might
be overwhelmed at the Fort.)

*  Killed by Yeenoghu, summoned by a water demon one round after I
dipped a potion in a fountain.  Thanks to a wand of wishing randomly
placed in Sokoban, I had GDSM and an AC around -19, but he just
casually paralyzed me and whacked away like he was playing T-ball.
What kills me is that I'd been wearing a nice oilskin cloak for almost
the entire game, but when I was killed I had wrapped my permanently-
invisible self with a mummy wrapping in order to interact with a
shopkeeper, and had forgotten to put the cloak back on.

*  Poisoned to death by an ordinary potion.  This was after dipping my
Valk's longsword in around ten fountains, drying them all up without
getting Excalibur, then later falling through a trap door into a Big
Room.  Running out of options while searching for the upstairs as the
denizens closed in, I quaffed an undentified potion, hoping it would
heal me.  The opposite happened.


